# Two runners (GitHub Actions + local Task Scheduler) append to the same note
# files. Appends at the same spot are not a real disagreement -- keeping both
# sides is always right -- so let git settle them instead of conflicting and
# wedging the unattended run.
*.md merge=union

# README.md is NOT union-mergeable: it carries a single entry-count line and a
# fixed-length "Latest additions" list, which union would duplicate. It is
# regenerated from the note files on every run, so sync() just rebuilds it.
README.md -merge

# used.json is NOT union-mergeable either: concatenating JSON lines yields
# invalid JSON, which would crash the next run. sync() union-merges it as data.
.content/used.json -merge
